{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/762898-homerule-for-xp-into-gift-conversion","id":762898,"title":"Homerule for XP into Gift conversion.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-11T00:54:44-08:00","id":762898,"title":"Homerule for XP into Gift conversion.","content":"One of the most difficult things I have had problems with is how xp becomes a gift. Xp isn't supposed to be a real force, so I prefer to suggest a personal rule where Permanent Gnosis, and unspent xp that is ear marked for another Gnosis valence, gets broken down and attuned to the spiritual knowledge that becomes your new Gift. Thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-11T01:02:39-08:00","id":762903,"title":"","content":"What? So how do you break it down by rank, give an example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-11T02:07:51-08:00","id":762932,"title":"","content":"XP becomes Gifts... just like XP becomes any learned trait that requires XP. Gifts are just &quot;taught&quot; in a very specific fashion that is (if spirit to Garou) nothing like regular learning, but they're still something a Garou has to go out and learn from a spirit.<br /> <br /> So the initial premise here seems hard to get past. There's a clearly defined way in the game that explains what the learning process is; with XP simply being a pacing mechanism to dictate how fast you can build up traits. Tying it to Gnosis seems extremely questionable, since Gnosis is extremely poorly defined in terms of how you raise it. I don't understand how tying Gifts to Gnosis is supposed to result in more clarity on how XP turns into Gifts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-11T02:09:30-08:00","id":762934,"title":"","content":"Erm. Experience is time, effort and skill. Gaining a new Gift means you find a spirit, talk it into teaching you, spend some time practicing it with it, and presto you have a new gift. It has been explained that the half spiritual nature of the Garou allows them to internalise specialised powers that stem from thematical progenitors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-11T02:13:10-08:00","id":762937,"title":"","content":"In our LARP we have a php/SQL based character management system. It calculates a gift guidance value. It states how likely it is that spirits will bestow a gift on you (if you petition for it). For every 12 XP spend on other traits you may spend 3 XP on a favoured gift. Not-favoured gifts count as three favoured gifts.<br /> <br /> The reasoning behind this is that gifts often bring a huge effect-to-xp trade-off, especially if the gift has no cost and no roll, because it doesn't depend on other traits at higher levels. So, we wanted to prohibit players from learning only gifts after they gain rank, but also raise other traits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-11T09:16:02-08:00","id":763169,"title":"","content":"I'm curious as to whether your LARP uses the core rules, or the MET rules in these regards.<br /> <br /> Though I'd find a lot of players probably wouldn't like how drawn out this makes learning Gifts. If my players get 4 XP a session, it means they can get one Rank 1 Gift a month of play (assuming we even get it once a week). If there's a non-favored they want... it's almost three months of play to get it.<br /> <br /> And that assumes they're always spending all their XP.<br /> <br /> It seems a fairly large roadblock for something that basically takes a bit of effort in finding the right Chiminage, and then an hour with a spirit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-11T09:38:03-08:00","id":763181,"title":"","content":"We use tabletop core rules for our character stats, but have developed a buy system for character creation, rather than dispersing dots by categories.<br /> <br /> Actually the system doesn't make it's calculation on spent experience, but total experience (spent, and not spent).<br /> <br /> Also, it isn't a yes/no kind of thing that players see, when they log in, but a 'X' on a green-to-red-colourline. As STs we see one of four stages if a player wants to add a gift to his character:<ul><li>&quot;sure&quot;</li> <li>&quot;okay, but spirit will inform character that this is the last boon from spirits for some time&quot;</li> <li>&quot;only if the character makes a compelling argument to the spirit AND the player impresses with his suggested depicting of the gift learning&quot; and</li> <li>&quot;hell no&quot;.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> In addition, unless they read this post, the players (and most of mx co-STs) probably don't know how the 'X' is placed on the colourbar. I told those who asked, and discussed it with those who are interested in the rules, but never publicly wrote the algorithm down. We however allowed for a merit and a flaw that allow for more or lesser gifts than our system usually allows.<br /> There is a &quot;not more than two gifts between two games&quot; rule, in addition to the gift guidance value. Simply so that players not keep large amounts of XP unspent and have sudden increases in their magical power once they gain a rank. We also allow for no more than two rites or three rite levels worth or rite learning per downtime. Meaning that for level four or five rites one had to spend the downtimes between three games in regular contact with a teacher.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1008,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","user":"heinrich","date":". 11-11-2015, 02:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-11T10:25:24-08:00","id":763218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/762898-homerule-for-xp-into-gift-conversion?p=762903#post762903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What? So how do you break it down by rank, give an example.</div> </div> </div> </div> Regardless of the Rank, you take the xp cost and subtract it from the spiritual muscle of your Gnosis, including unspent xp that could have gone to buying Gnosis. If a Gift costs 9 xp and your spiritual life's experiences and exercises have achieved a spiritual &quot;muscle mass&quot; of 5 Gnosis, then you go down to 4 Gnosis plus one xp that gets spent on rebuilding that spiritual valence. <br /> <br /> I think of it as being similar to attuning to a fetish but permanent as your are using that spiritual strength that creates the rapport between you and this specific knowledge of the spirit world rather than just a general attunement that Gnosis represents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-11T11:06:43-08:00","id":763257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/762898-homerule-for-xp-into-gift-conversion?p=763218#post763218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Regardless of the Rank, you take the xp cost and subtract it from the spiritual muscle of your Gnosis, including unspent xp that could have gone to buying Gnosis. If a Gift costs 9 xp and your spiritual life's experiences and exercises have achieved a spiritual &quot;muscle mass&quot; of 5 Gnosis, then you go down to 4 Gnosis plus one xp that gets spent on rebuilding that spiritual valence.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> This is worse than common core math. It seems like you are trying to come up with a way to make gifts cheaper for high-Gnosis werewolves... but Gnosis is already a pretty important stat. Your whole reason for wanting such a system is to avoid using the abstraction of xp, yet xp is still very much a factor in your system. <a href=\"https://memecrunch.com/image/509852c2afa96f2d52000009.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">Your method does not cost xp directly, but then you have to buy up your Gnosis again?</a><br /> <br /> <br /> I really think this house rule lacks clarity and does not succeed in even meeting its objective of doing away with xp.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3695,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","user":"The Laughing Stranger","date":". 11-11-2015, 02:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-11T11:56:23-08:00","id":763306,"title":"","content":"You have to &quot;exercise&quot; to get Gnosis, you have to spend a few hours with a spirit to get a Gift. One is muscle that you work for, sort of, the other isn't. I figure that this works because Garou are intensely spiritual beings, and their spiritual mindfulness and dedication to the spirits should always be a good reason to build up your spiritual side.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-11T14:14:42-08:00","id":763449,"title":"","content":"In In nomine it flat out says a lot of your char points are Direct improvements an archangel makes to a servitor as a reward for a job well done... would something like here be appropiate?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-11T14:19:22-08:00","id":763455,"title":"","content":"I'm gonna have to say nope, that house rule is kinda lame.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-11T16:09:07-08:00","id":763559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/762898-homerule-for-xp-into-gift-conversion?p=763449#post763449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div 